WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.509
Welcome to MIT's Autonomous Robotics&nbsp;
Team Arcturus

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.296
Arcturus!

00:00:05.876 --> 00:00:07.331
Arcturus!

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:13.560
Arcturus was just founded in 2022 but we've&nbsp;already made waves. During our first year as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:18.060
team in the robo boat competition Arcturus came&nbsp;in third place in the design portion and fourth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.620
place in the autonomous challenge. This season&nbsp;we're building two boats and a submarine all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:28.140
which will be autonomous. We're looking to compete&nbsp;in Robo Boat 2023 in Sarasota Florida and the Nord&nbsp;Challenge

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:32.760
in Trondheim Norway. Our mission&nbsp;is to provide undergraduates with practical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.500
hands-on experience engineering large systems.Arcturus presents an incredible opportunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.860
for students to learn the fundamentals&nbsp;
of applied engineering and manufacturing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.360
through Arcturus students are able to&nbsp;
gain engineering experience outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:50.466
of the classroom while learning to work&nbsp;
with others and guide their own projects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.524 --> 00:00:52.008
My name is Audrey and I'm the captain of&nbsp;
Arcturus. 

00:00:52.008 --> 00:00:58.380
Arcturus has split into three&nbsp;separate sub teams: mechanical, navigations, and electrical. Let's meet&nbsp;them now

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:01.449
Hi I'm Jessica and I'm Jared and we're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:05.385
the mechanical design team leads, of all the&nbsp;mechanical systems as well as the structure of&nbsp;the hull

00:01:06.286 --> 00:01:10.920
Our general workflow starts with design&nbsp;parts and On Shape which is a cloud-based software&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.140
that allows us to collaborate throughout the&nbsp;design process of the boat. From there we move on to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:25.082
assembly and fabrication, we use a couple of tools like 3D printing, milling and laser printing. This allows us to create custom parts for us to test and iterate.&nbsp;

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:30.766
Hi everyone my name is Herbie, I'm a master's student and I lead the navigation sub team.&nbsp;

00:01:30.766 --> 00:01:32.400
We're responsible for all the software&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:40.380
that goes on the boat and we're split into several&nbsp;sub teams-- perception, path planning and mapping, and&nbsp;embedded

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:47.445
We primarily use ROS, the Robot Operating&nbsp;System which is a middleware software commonly&nbsp;used for robotics

00:01:48.576 --> 00:01:54.291
Hi my name is Ansel and I'm&nbsp;
one of the electronics leads for MIT Arcturus

00:01:54.291 --> 00:01:58.260
we deal with the entire electrical subsystem&nbsp;for the boat. Starting from the early design&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:02.940
stages we go in and develop all of the smaller&nbsp;subsystem circuits, getting a test rig set up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:06.180
to verify them on the bench and then we&nbsp;
integrate them into the vessel at large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.860
once it's all hooked up we do a full vehicle&nbsp;systems test and that's our final step

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:18.060
from late night sleepovers watching SharkBoy and&nbsp;Lavagirl to Robo parties at every test launch we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:22.500
know that building is always more fun in good&nbsp;company. We're growing rapidly and just this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.720
year our little family has tripled in size to 40&nbsp;members. We're continuing to learn more and more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.560
each day and we couldn't be more excited to show&nbsp;off all of our hard work at competition this year

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.060
[Music]

